From: Mathieu <mlaparie@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: simple: agc: settle the exposure faster

The automatic exposure moved by kExpProportionalGain (0.04) times the
error, at most kExpMaxStep (0.15) per step; with the error at most about
2.5, steps were near 10 %, and a step waits for the previous one to reach
the sensor.  Going from the 10 ms of a dark start to the 66 ms the soft
IPA now allows (patch 0018) took seconds (author, 2026-11-02: exposure
very long to stabilise).  0.12 and 0.4: about three times as fast.

Ours (fxtec-pro1x-guix), on top of moWerk's 0012 and our 0018.

(from mlaparie/fxtec-pro1x-guix device/libcamera/af, next branch)
---
diff --git a/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/agc.cpp b/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/agc.cpp
index c00710a..583ddcb 100644
--- a/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/agc.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/agc.cpp
@@ -53,13 +53,13 @@ static constexpr float kExposureSatisfactory = 0.2;
  * This replaces the fixed 10% bang-bang step with a proportional correction
  * that converges smoothly and avoids overshooting near the target.
  */
-static constexpr float kExpProportionalGain = 0.04;
+static constexpr float kExpProportionalGain = 0.12;
 
 /*
  * Maximum multiplicative step per frame, to bound the correction when the
  * scene changes dramatically.
  */
-static constexpr float kExpMaxStep = 0.15;
+static constexpr float kExpMaxStep = 0.4;
 
 Agc::Agc()
 {
